File: maxima-core-docs.info,  Node: Function quantile_exp q m,  Next: Function quantile_f q m n,  Prev: Function quantile_discrete_uniform q n,  Up: distrib

 -- Function: quantile_exp (Q, M)
     Returns the _q_-quantile of an {\it Exponential}(m) random
     variable, with m>0; in other words, this is the inverse of
     ‘cdf_exp’.  Argument _q_ must be an element of [0,1].

     The {\it Exponential}(m) random variable is equivalent to the {\it
     Weibull}(1,1/m) .

     (%i1) load ("distrib")$
     
     (%i2) quantile_exp(0.56,5);
     (%o2)                  0.1641961104139661
     
     
     (%i3) quantile_exp(0.56,m);
                            0.8209805520698303
     (%o3)                  ------------------
                                    m


