File: maxima-core-docs.info,  Node: Function quantile_geometric q p,  Next: Function quantile_gumbel q a b,  Prev: Function quantile_general_finite_discrete q v,  Up: distrib

 -- Function: quantile_geometric (Q, P)
     Returns the _q_-quantile of a {\it Geometric}(p) random variable,
     with 0 \lt p \le 1 ; in other words, this is the inverse of
     ‘cdf_geometric’.  Argument _q_ must be an element of [0,1].

     The probability from which the quantile is derived is defined as p
     (1 - p)^x.  This is interpreted as the probability of x failures
     before the first success.

     ‘load("distrib")’ loads this function.


