     Returns the _q_-quantile of a {\it Normal}(m, s) random variable,
     with s>0; in other words, this is the inverse of ‘cdf_normal’.
     Argument _q_ must be an element of [0,1].  To make use of this
     function, write first ‘load("distrib")’.

     (%i1) load ("distrib")$
     
     (%i2) quantile_normal(95/100,0,1);
                                              9
     (%o2)                sqrt(2) inverse_erf(--)
                                              10
     
     
     (%i3) float(%);
     (%o3)                  1.6448536269514724

     See also: ‘cdf_normal’.


