 -- Function: std_rayleigh (B)
     Returns the standard deviation of a {\it Rayleigh}(b) random
     variable, with b>0.

     The {\it Rayleigh}(b) random variable is equivalent to the {\it
     Weibull}(2,1/b) .

     The standard deviation is

     D[X] = {1\over b}\sqrt{\displaystyle 1 - {\pi\over 4}}

     (%i1) load ("distrib")$
     
     (%i2) std_rayleigh(b);
